      "bottomRightY": 239,
      "content": "### 2.1 Overview",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 81,
      "topLeftY": 248,
      "bottomRightX": 636,
      "bottomRightY": 315,
      "content": "The goal of GenTL is to provide an agnostic transport layer interface to acquire images or other data and to communicate with a device. It is not its purpose to configure the device except for the transport related features – even if it must be indirectly used in order to communicate configuration information to and from the device.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 81,
      "topLeftY": 329,
      "bottomRightX": 253,
      "bottomRightY": 346,
      "content": "#### 2.1.1 GenICam GenTL",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "title"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 81,
      "topLeftY": 351,
      "bottomRightX": 636,
      "bottomRightY": 401,
      "content": "The standard text's primary concern is the definition of the GenTL Interface and its behavior. However, it is also important to understand the role of the GenTL in the whole GenICam system.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
