    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 81,
      "topLeftY": 690,
      "bottomRightX": 636,
      "bottomRightY": 724,
      "content": "When used alone, GenTL is used to identify two different entities: the GenTL Producer and the GenTL Consumer.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 81,
      "topLeftY": 731,
      "bottomRightX": 636,
      "bottomRightY": 782,
      "content": "A GenTL Producer is a software driver implementing the GenTL Interface to enable an application or a software library to access and configure hardware in a generic way and to stream image data from a device.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 81,
      "topLeftY": 788,
      "bottomRightX": 636,
      "bottomRightY": 823,
      "content": "A GenTL Consumer is any software that can use one or multiple GenTL Producers via the defined GenTL Interface. This can be for example an application or a software library.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
